# The Trapper's cost taps "another untapped creature you control" (CR 118.3): with only the Trapper, which is tapped by its own {T}, there is
# none, so attempting the ability rolls back although Mox Ruby's {1} and a target (Bot2's Ornithopter) are there. The positive control is
# wanderbrine-trapper-taps-an-opponents-creature-by-tapping-a-summoning-sick-creature-of-yours.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Wanderbrine Trapper
Island x4
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Wanderbrine Trapper.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Wanderbrine Trapper.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Choose(Tap Wanderbrine Trapper)
? Bot1.Mana = {R}
? Bot1.ManaFrom = {R} Mox Ruby
? Bot1.Life = 20
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
? Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Wanderbrine Trapper.Tapped = false
